WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.960
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
This week, we're

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.390
talking about security, core
performance, and machine

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:03.945
learning.

00:00:03.945 --> 00:00:05.820
Welcome to This Week in
Cloud, where we serve

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.039
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:08.039 --> 00:00:10.110
Google Cloud is already
known for great security,

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.110
but we're excited to take that
even further with Chronicle

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.850
joining the Google Cloud family.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.893
This means more tools, such as
malware intelligence services,

00:00:17.893 --> 00:00:19.560
will be available to
use with your cloud

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.560
infrastructure and your
data, enabling you to detect

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.630
and mitigate threats faster.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.280
Read more about the
details and prepare

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.470
to buff up your security.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.940
Investigating
production code just

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.250
got easier with
Stackdriver Profiler now

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.600
generally available.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.695
Profiler lets you look at
how your code runs and breaks

00:00:36.695 --> 00:00:38.070
down where time
and resources are

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.023
being spent with no
noticeable performance impact.

00:00:41.023 --> 00:00:43.440
There was a great session from
Google Cloud Next with more

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.540
details, so check
it out and start

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.910
improving your production code.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.950
BigQuery is now
integrated with Kaggle,

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:53.730
making it easier and faster to
analyze data and train models.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.070
Kaggle is where the world's
largest online community

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.810
of data scientists
come together,

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.930
and it offers tools like
kernels, a free hosted Jupyter

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.370
notebooks environment.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.739
These two great tools are
even greater when integrated,

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:08.100
so start by linking your account
and try out the new tutorials

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.525
to query like never before.

00:01:10.525 --> 00:01:13.150
It can take a lot of time to set
up a machine learning project,

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.900
especially with managing the
complexity and compatibility

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.780
issues of an ever
evolving software stack.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.030
When you'd rather just spend
time refining your model,

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.710
deep learning containers
are a great place to start.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.230
These containers
are prepackaged,

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:28.000
performance optimized,
and compatibility tested.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.870
So you have a consistent
environment to work in.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:33.930
Follow along with the tutorial
and use the beta deep learning

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.047
containers to get
to the fun stuff.

00:01:36.047 --> 00:01:38.130
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.230
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.460
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.360
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.830
We'll see you in the cloud.

